    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0699" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.6363/830: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-14T10:00:00-04:00">May 14, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1082. Your 1214 of May 11, 9 a.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d618-f1"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Loading authorization is being granted by the Department and Board of
                        Economic Warfare on May 19–20 for the five tankers named in your 1086, April
                        29, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="36" xml:id="d618-f2"/> in view of possible
                        misunderstanding by the Spanish Government.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I remain of the opinion expressed in paragraph 3 of the Department’s 1033,
                        May 6, noon.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d618-f3"/> Loading authorization for the
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Zorroza</hi> for the early June loading date
                        will therefore not be granted by the Department and Board of Economic
                        Warfare. Accordingly, please arrange for the postponement of its departure
                        from Spain.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>It occurs to me from my reading of your recent telegrams that you may not
                        be giving full weight to the importance of public opinion and judgement here
                        which I believe would view most unfavorably any increase in the actual
                        shipment of oil to Spain over that of the highest quarter of 1942. Indeed,
                        despite the care with which we are following the matter, there is more
                        criticism of this oil program to Spain than of any other matter of foreign
                        policy under my direction. I have agreed to the loading of the five tankers
                        (which will bring the second quarter shipments well above the first quarter
                        rate) because the sailing authorizations leave me no alternative, but I do
                        not wish any further authorization for second quarter sailings to be given,
                        and I regard it of utmost importance that the prescriptions from the
                        Department respecting all tanker movements be scrupulously adhered
                        to.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
